  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 2501.01 Statement of Purpose. The division of plant industry of the New Hampshire department of agriculture, markets and food is charged with the function of nursery stock inspection and regulation under the immediate supervision of the state entomologist and commissioner of agriculture. The purpose of these rules is to clarify the procedures and methods used for licensure, compliance agreements, and issuance of export certificates, and used by inspectors of the division of plant industry in dealing with infections, diseases, and insect pests of nursery stock.\n\nSource. #5359, eff 3-17-92; ss by #6708, eff 3-4-98, EXPIRED: 3-4-06\n\nNew. #9323, eff 11-21-08; ss by #12114, eff 2-21-17",
